               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 69-year-old female patient, admitted on 04/03/1990 with acute lower abdominal pain and suspected tubal pregnancy. On admission, physical examination revealed hemodynamic stability with mild peritoneal irritation in the right lower quadrant. Transvaginal ultrasonography confirmed an ectopic tubal pregnancy with no signs of free intraperitoneal hemorrhage. Serum beta-hCG levels were significantly elevated, corroborating the diagnosis. Given the patient's age, clinical presentation, and risk of rupture, a decision was made for surgical intervention. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy for removal of the ectopic tubal pregnancy, which proceeded without complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Wound care and vital sign monitoring were maintained throughout the stay. The patient was discharged in stable condition on 10/03/1990. Please ensure appropriate outpatient follow-up.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
